# Crafting Recipe Creator

This plan details the addition of a crafting recipe editor to the Minecraft Mod Maker, allowing users to define how their custom blocks and items are created using standard Minecraft materials.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The recipe system will specifically support **Shaped Crafting** (3x3 grid). 
> I will provide a searchable list of approximately 100+ common Minecraft blocks/items (Iron, Diamond, Oak Logs, etc.) to use as ingredients. For anything missing, you will be able to manually type the ID.

## Proposed Changes

### Data Model

#### [NEW] [Recipe.java](file:///home/vladimir/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/minecraft_mod_maker/src/main/java/com/modmaker/Recipe.java)
- A simple class containing a 3x3 array of `String` (Minecraft IDs).

#### [MODIFY] [BlockData.java](file:///home/vladimir/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/minecraft_mod_maker/src/main/java/com/modmaker/BlockData.java) & [ItemData.java](file:///home/vladimir/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/minecraft_mod_maker/src/main/java/com/modmaker/ItemData.java)
- Add a `Recipe` field to these classes and update their constructors.

### UI Components

#### [MODIFY] [ModMakerApp.java](file:///home/vladimir/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/minecraft_mod_maker/src/main/java/com/modmaker/ModMakerApp.java)
- **Crafting Grid Panel**: Create a internal method to build a 3x3 grid of `JButton`s.
- **Item Selector Sidebar**: A list of common Minecraft items (e.g., `minecraft:iron_ingot`, `minecraft:stick`).
- **Interactive Logic**: 
    - Selecting an item from the list sets the "Current Ingredient".
    - Clicking a slot in the 3x3 grid assigns that ingredient to the slot.
    - Right-clicking or a "Clear" tool clears a slot.
- **Integration**: Insert this panel into both the "Add Block" and "Add Item" tabs.

### Generator Logic

#### [MODIFY] [ModGenerator.java](file:///home/vladimir/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/minecraft_mod_maker/src/main/java/com/modmaker/ModGenerator.java)
- Implement `createRecipes(File workDir, String modId, List<ModElement> elements)`:
    - Iterates through elements.
    - If a recipe is defined, generate a JSON file in `src/main/resources/data/<modid>/recipes/<element_name>.json`.
    - Correctly maps the 3x3 grid to the Forge "pattern", "key", and "result" format.

## Open Questions

- Should I include a "Crafting Result Count" (e.g., crafting 1 block gives you 4 items)? I plan to default it to 1 for now.
- Is a searchable list of ~100 common items sufficient for the "All Blocks" requirement, or do you need a more exhaustive list?

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
1.  Open the App.
2.  Create a custom block.
3.  Define a recipe (e.g., 3 iron ingots in a row).
4.  Generate the Mod.
5.  Inspect the generated JAR's `data` folder to ensure the recipe JSON exists and is correctly formatted.
